[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":96},"routes/item",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10},"item",{"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":20,"_21":22,"_23":24,"_25":26,"_27":28,"_29":28,"_30":31,"_32":33,"_34":35,"_36":37,"_38":39,"_40":-5,"_41":-5,"_42":43,"_44":-5,"_45":46,"_47":48,"_49":50,"_51":52,"_53":37,"_54":37,"_55":-5,"_56":37,"_57":58},"expiresAt",1795826454000,"id","wcbx8pzdh8mopdy9bq9yswr42","title","Microsoft 与 CSA 披露 ARTEX AI 攻击框架已被多组攻击者采用","originalTitle","Chinese, North Korean Hackers Adopt ARTEX AI Offensive Framework","summary","Microsoft 与 CSA 报告称，中国及朝鲜关联攻击组织已将开源 AI 自主渗透测试框架 ARTEX 用于网络侦察、凭据攻击和 Web 应用利用，部分攻击链可在 3 小时内取得特权访问，Infrawatch 则发现野外存在 130 多个变种。","reason","文章汇总多方对 ARTEX 框架的观测，说明其自动化攻击链与规避检测能力，并列出可供防守方落实的资产、身份和出站控制措施。","source",{"_66":95},"links",{"_86":94},"publishedAt","2026-11-26T11:05:00.000Z","discoveredAt","2026-11-26T11:41:23.732Z","timelineAt","category","activity","tags",[69,71,67,91,92,93],"score",70,"selected",true,"channel","news","story","x","readingMode","full","author","body",{"_58":85,"_86":-5,"_87":88,"_89":90},"outline",[76,77],"relatedStories",[],"topics",[59,60,61,62,63],"indexable","markdownAvailable","group","hasTranslation","bodyLanguage","zh",{"_64":74,"_66":75},{"_64":72,"_66":73},{"_64":70,"_66":71},{"_64":68,"_66":69},{"_64":65,"_66":67},"slug","malware","name","恶意软件","attack","攻击活动","ai-offense","AI 攻防","supply-chain","供应链安全","microsoft","Microsoft / 微软",{"_11":83,"_79":84,"_81":82},{"_11":78,"_79":80,"_81":82},"sec-2","text","How to Protect Against ARTEX-Driven Attacks","level",2,"sec-1","攻击者如何部署 ARTEX","<p><img src=\"/dailyinfo/media/6a795d301a355173.webp\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Photo of James Coker\"></p><p>\n\t关于 ARTEX 被用于网络攻击活动的报道：</p><ul>\n\t<li>\n\t\t<a href=\"https://www.infosecurity-magazine.com/news/commission-ai-attack-systems/\"><em>欧盟委员会确认由 AI 驱动的网络攻击导致系统离线</em></a></li>\n\t<li>\n\t\t<a href=\"https://www.infosecurity-magazine.com/news/microsoft-chinese-ai-connectwise/\"><em>微软：中国国家行为体使用 AI 攻破 ConnectWave 租户</em></a></li>\n\t<li>\n\t\t<a href=\"https://www.infosecurity-magazine.com/news/chinese-hacker-ai-korean-banks/\"><em>中国黑客在针对韩国银行的行动中部署了 AI</em></a></li>\n</ul><p>\n\t新的研究报告记录显示，ARTEX AI 攻击框架目前已被广泛部署于网络活动中，使国家行为体和网络犯罪团伙都能使用。 &nbsp;</p><p>\n\t该工具已与近几个月来的多起备受关注的事件相关联，关于其使用的更多信息也在不断出现。</p><p>\n\t微软 <a href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/11/25/what-defenders-need-to-know-artex-agentic-ai-framework-threat-actors-abuse/\">披露</a>，11 月 25 日有多个中国和朝鲜国家组织已将 ARTEX 集成到其工具集中。</p><p>\n\t这家科技巨头表示，其观察到与中国有关联的行为体 <a href=\"https://www.infosecurity-magazine.com/news/chinese-tech-firms-salt-typhoon/\">Salt Typhoon</a>、Crystal Typhoon、Storm-0940 和 Storm-3358 在攻击活动中利用 ARTEX，此外还有与朝鲜民主主义人民共和国（DPRK）有关联的行为体 <a href=\"https://www.infosecurity-magazine.com/news/north-korean-exploiting-critical/\">Onyx Sleet</a> 和 Pearl Sleet。</p><p>\n\t上述组织利用该框架自动化了攻击链的各个阶段，包括网络侦察、凭据攻击和 Web 应用漏洞利用。</p><p>\n\t与此同时，云安全联盟（CSA）<a href=\"https://cloudsecurityalliance.org/artifacts/aof\">报告</a>（同样于 11 月 25 日发布）将 ARTEX 和 Cairn 等智能体化攻击框架（AOF）的出现描述为 AI 驱动网络安全威胁的“第三波”。</p><p>\n\t报告指出，这些框架显著加快了攻击链的速度，在某些情况下使威胁行为体能够在不到三小时内获得特权访问。这些工具让行为体能够系统性地探测攻击面、串联漏洞，并快速执行并发的内网横向移动。</p><p>\n\tCSA 补充称，ARTEX 使资源有限的犯罪分子也能实施复杂的攻击链。</p><p>\n\t报告称：“尽管这些攻击在理论上此前就已可能实现，但我们现在看到威胁行为体已大规模部署了它们。”</p><p>\n\tInfrawatch 于 11 月 24 日发布的<a href=\"https://infrawatch.com/blog/the-autonomy-of-the-autonomous-intrusions\">分析</a>强调了野外存在超过 130 个 ARTEX 变体。</p><p>\n\t这家网络安全公司观察到，10 月入侵激增之后，11 月初 ARTEX 服务器数量急剧上升。</p><p>\n\t<a href=\"https://www.infosecurity-magazine.com/news/fbi-growing-abuse-ai-pentesting/\"><em>现在阅读：FBI 强调 AI 驱动的渗透测试框架 ARTEX 滥用日益严重</em></a></p><h2 id=\"sec-1\">\n\t<strong>攻击者如何部署 ARTEX</strong></h2><p>\n\t<a href=\"https://www.infosecurity-magazine.com/news/artex-activity-exceeds-reported/\">ARTEX</a> 是一个开源的、由 AI 模型驱动的自主渗透测试框架，由一位名为 ‘Autumn-27’ 的用户于 2026 年 7 月在 GitHub 上发布。</p><p>\n\tARTEX 使用 Go 编写，内嵌 Next.js Web 控制台，提供一个攻击性命令与控制（C2）平台，可与多个 AI 智能体通信，并可接入大语言模型（LLM）。</p><p>\n\t微软报告强调，ARTEX 并未引入新的攻击技术，而是使用常见的、已存在的渗透测试工具和技术。</p><p>\n\t然而，使用 ARTEX 的威胁行为体可以变换网络指标，如源 IP 地址或用户代理字符串，尤其是为了绕过静态或基于简单签名的检测与阻断。</p><p>\n\t微软解释，要部署该工具，威胁行为体会定义目标范围，然后由一个目标模型将整个行动分解为可验证的具体目标。</p><p>\n\t“Planner” and “worker” agents then work together in formulating and executing an attack cycle based on network reconnaissance undertaken on the target.</p><p>\n\tA reporter agent communicates the attack stages back to the threat actor with reproduction steps and a proof of concept.</p><figure><img src=\"/dailyinfo/media/8d375eeffcec8b40.webp\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"ARTEX AI agent deployment in campaigns. Source: Microsoft\"><figcaption>ARTEX AI agent deployment in campaigns. Source: Microsoft</figcaption></figure><p>\n\tARTEX contains a number of pre-configured tools that define its core capabilities, which are network reconnaissance, web application mapping, web shell upload and web browser-based attacks.</p><p>\n\tMicrosoft noted that threat actors can add arbitrary tools, such as credential attack tools, that can be used by ARTEX.</p><h2 id=\"sec-2\">\n\t<strong>How to Protect Against ARTEX-Driven Attacks</strong></h2><p>\n\tMicrosoft set out a number of recommendations for defenders to protect their organizations against ARTEX-driven attack campaigns. These include:</p><ul>\n\t<li>\n\t\tInventory internet-facing assets and prioritize fixes on resources that lead to sensitive data or privileged identities</li>\n\t<li>\n\t\tBlock and slow down attacks on web applications and APIs, such as capping how many requests one client can send in a short time</li>\n\t<li>\n\t\tMap what an exposed asset or stolen credential could reach before an agent does to enable faster response following a compromise</li>\n\t<li>\n\t\tRun endpoint protection on every internet-facing server and keep it blocking</li>\n\t<li>\n\t\tRestrict outbound connections from web servers, such as allowing only the destinations each server needs</li>\n\t<li>\n\t\tApply conditional access to every user and workload identity</li>\n\t<li>\n\t\tHarden and monitor the services that hold secrets and data</li>\n</ul>","original","zhKind","translation","complete",false,"供应链投毒","Agent 安全","Microsoft","https://www.infosecurity-magazine.com/news/chinese-north-korea-artex/","Infosecurity Magazine",{"_97":98,"_99":-5},"changelogVersion","2026-10-01T08:00","release"]
